From 2dcf12c956f931027dadc734a7279777fefaadb5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: operator <225459632+operator@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 16:10:11 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Four Sparks: WORKERS, patch 0010 (TP=4), the multirank wire's
 kernel

WORKERS lists ranks 1.. in order (default WORKER, so two Sparks are unchanged); start.sh, stop.sh,
prepare.sh, fetch_pack.sh and zig_prepare.sh run each step on every worker. patches-zig/0010 admits
four ranks in TensorFold; ZIG_TREE is v1.2.3 + 0001-0010. zig_prepare.sh also builds fabric/tp's
mailbox kernel, which start.sh passes at four Sparks with ROCE=1 (else NCCL carries every gather).

At two Sparks the build and scripts give byte-identical greedy replies to the previous recipe:
plain, drafted, and four streams at once.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
