+From a9de80c69a0d055cd161270ed2444e5023bb342d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
+From: operator <225459632+operator@users.noreply.github.com>
+Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 15:59:39 +0000
+Subject: [PATCH] ricursive: four ranks (TP=4) as well as one or two
+
+Admission takes 1, 2 or 4 ranks: 80 query heads, 8 key heads, the FFN, the vocabulary and the
+drafter all cut evenly at four, on whole 128-wide blocks. The forward, the header exchange, the
+follow loop, rankSum and the drafter were already written for any world.
+
+At four ranks TF_RICURSIVE_ROCE=1 opens fabric/tp's multirank wire for the small gathers (the
+same wire, probe and vote as GLM's cuda_roce_multi.zig); without its settings, or if any rank's
+probe differs from NCCL, every rank keeps NCCL. Two ranks keep their own RoCE wire.
+
+The family module imports fabric/tp; the native server shares GLM's instance, as one file
+belongs to one module.
+
+At two ranks the build is byte-identical to the previous one: greedy replies to four prompts,
+plain, drafted and four streams at once.
+
+Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
